X-SOURCE:Jack of the Wood
UID:11877@jackofthewood.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261030T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261030T233000
DTSTAMP:20260330T214216Z
URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/charming-disaster/
SUMMARY:Charming Disaster
DESCRIPTION:\nBrooklyn-based musical duo Charming Disaster was formed in 20
 12 by Ellia Bisker and Jeff Morris. Inspired by the gothic humor of Edward
  Gorey and Tim Burton\, the murder ballads of the Americana tradition\, an
 d the dramatic flair of the cabaret\, they write songs that tell stories\,
  using two voices to explore dark narratives and characters with a playful
 ly macabre sensibility. \n\n\n\nIn their interactive Musical Oracle show\,
  songs are selected by chance by audience members who draw cards from the 
 Charming Disaster Oracle Deck—a Tarot-style divination that straddles th
 e line between concert and theatre. \n\n\n\nCharming Disaster has released
  seven critically acclaimed albums: Love\, Crime &amp\; Other Trouble (201
 5)\, Cautionary Tales (2017)\, SPELLS + RITUALS (2019)\, Our Lady of Radiu
 m (2022)\, Super Natural History (2023)\, singles collection Time Ghost (2
 024)\, and The Double (2025). In their songs\, the duo have explored love\
 , death\, crime\, folklore\, mythology\, magic\, science\, and the occult.
  Their theatrical live performances combine vocal harmonies and clever lyr
 ics with ukulele\, guitar\, and virtuosic foot percussion\, drawing listen
 ers into a spooky\, offbeat universe of paranormal romance\, con artists\,
  circus performers\, ancient mythology\, nightclubs\, car chases\, the aft
 erlife\, and beyond. \n\n\n\nCharming Disaster’s music has been featured
  on the podcast Welcome to Night Vale\, they have opened for legendary cel
 lo-rock ensemble Rasputina\, goth icon Voltaire\, and punk cabaret duo The
  Dresden Dolls\, and their theatrical\, entertaining live performances hav
 e captivated audiences across the United States and Europe. They have play
 ed festivals\, bars and clubs\, museums and art galleries\, bookstores and
  libraries\, and the occasional historic cemetery. They have appeared alon
 gside storytellers\, comedians\, fire eaters\, puppets\, burlesque artists
 \, poets\, and circus performers. Recent appearances include the Meadowlar
 k Festival\, the Rochester Fringe Festival\, Dragon Con\, Joe’s Pub at T
 he Public Theater in NYC\, Brooklyn’s historic Green-Wood Cemetery\, Phi
 ladelphia’s Science History Institute\, the Edgar Allan Poe Museum in Ri
 chmond\, VA\, Cleveland’s Wizbang Theatre\, and the Coney Island Sidesho
 w stage.Music 8:30-11:30pm\, $10 cover at the door.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps
 ://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TAjqTD8kFNI\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://www.yout
 ube.com/watch?v=BNIzpoFj4a0&amp\;t=20s\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/01/Charmingdisaster1.webp
END:VEVENT
